-- title:
--   From HTo G Sum Finsets By Card Indicator
-- statement:
--   **Grouping support sets by size yields the operator-valued binomial tail.**
--
--   Let $G$ be an operator and let $d,k\in\mathbb N$. Group the subset expansion by the cardinality of the support set. The exact finite identity is
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{s\subseteq[k]}
--   \begin{cases}
--   G^{|s|}(I-G)^{k-|s|},&d+1\le |s|,\\
--   0,&d+1>|s|
--   \end{cases}
--   =
--   \sum_{r\in[d+1,k]}
--   \binom{k}{r}\,G^r(I-G)^{k-r},
--   $$
--
--   where the interval sum is empty when its lower endpoint exceeds its upper endpoint. The scalar binomial coefficient acts on the operator by complex scalar multiplication. This is the combinatorial step that identifies the terminal type sum with the operator-valued Bernoulli tail.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_sum_finsets_by_card_indicator`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
